Implementations Directory Structure
===================================

Algorithm: COMPASS-KEM (Key Encapsulation Mechanism)

This directory contains reference, optimized, and additional implementations
of the COMPASS-KEM algorithm for the Next-generation Commercial Cryptographic
Algorithms Program (NGCC).

Directory Overview
------------------

Reference_Implementation/
    Reference implementation in ISO C (C99), without platform-specific
    instruction set dependencies. This implementation prioritizes clarity
    and correctness over performance.

    Algorithm Instances:
      - COMPASS-KEM-128  (128-bit classical security, K=2, N=256, Q=3329)
      - COMPASS-KEM-256  (256-bit classical security, K=4, N=256, Q=3329)
      - COMPASS-KEM-384  (384-bit classical security, K=3, N=512, Q=7681)
      - COMPASS-KEM-512  (512-bit classical security, K=4, N=512, Q=7681)

Optimized_Implementation/
    Optimized implementation targeting mainstream 64-bit PC processors.
    Uses AVX2 vector instructions and platform-specific optimizations.

Additional_Implementation/
    Reserved for additional platform implementations (e.g., 32-bit embedded
    systems, hardware implementations).

File Descriptions (Common Source Files)
----------------------------------------

Core KEM:
    kem.h / kem.c               CCA-secure KEM: key generation, encapsulation,
                                decapsulation (Fujisaki-Okamoto transform)
    indcpa.h / indcpa.c         IND-CPA-secure public key encryption scheme

Polynomial Arithmetic:
    poly.h / poly.c             Polynomial operations: compression, decompression,
                                NTT, inverse NTT, message encoding/decoding
    polyvec.h / polyvec.c       Polynomial vector operations: pointwise multiply,
                                addition, compression, decompression
    ntt.h / ntt.c               Number Theoretic Transform (NTT) implementation
    reduce.h / reduce.c         Barrett and Montgomery modular reduction
    cbd.h / cbd.c               Centered Binomial Distribution (CBD) sampling

Symmetric Primitives:
    symmetric.h                 Symmetric operation macros (hash, XOF, PRF)
    symmetric-shake.c           SHAKE-based PRF implementations

Auxiliary:
    fips202.h / fips202.c       FIPS 202 (SHA3 / SHAKE / Keccak) implementation
    verify.h / verify.c         Constant-time comparison and conditional move
    randombytes.h / randombytes.c  Platform-specific random byte generation

NGCC Submission Framework Files (provided by ICCS, DO NOT MODIFY):
    drng.h / drng.c             Deterministic Random Number Generator (SM3-based)
    auxfunc.h / auxfunc.c       Auxiliary hash/XOF functions (SM3-based)
    KAT_KEM.c                   Known Answer Test (KAT) vector generation tool

NGCC API Adapter (modified by submitter):
    KEM_AlgorithmInstance.h     NGCC programming interface (kem_keygen/enc/dec)
    KEM_AlgorithmInstance.c     API bridge: maps NGCC API to internal KEM API
    params.h                    Algorithm parameters for all security levels
    api.h                       Internal API size constants and function prototypes

Build and Test:
    Makefile                    Automated build script (test, speed, KAT generation)
    README.txt                  NGCC framework usage instructions
    test/                       Test and benchmark programs

Notes
-----
- This submission targets the NGCC program (商用密码标准研究院).
- Cryptographic hash and XOF functions use the ICCS-provided auxiliary
  functions (auxfunc.h/c) in compliance with submission requirements.
- The DRNG (drng.h/c) is used for deterministic test vector generation.
- All code is written in ISO C99 with GCC/Clang compatibility.
